## Entry 3 — Sprint 3: Application Resumes and Seeker Dashboard

**Date:** November 9–11, 2026
**Team Member:** Ayza
**AI Tool:** Cursor
**Sprint:** 3
**Purpose:** Keep each submitted resume with its application and show the seeker's application activity.

### Task

I used Cursor for the Sprint 3 seeker work assigned at the November 5 kickoff: link the resume used on an application, show application history, and show status counts and activity statistics.

### Prompt / Summary

The original Cursor chat was not exported. The committed result is the record of what was kept.

### AI Output Summary

Cursor stored a copy of the resume submitted with each application, so replacing the profile resume does not change older applications. It added an application details page, weekly application counts, and the seeker dashboard statistics. Automated tests were added for the resume link, the metrics, and the Sprint 3 acceptance checks.

### Action Taken

**Accepted with review**

The change was committed as `a3551b5`. On November 11 I demonstrated the application and seeker-dashboard work. The team later kept the existing statistics and did not add extra graphs in Sprint 3.

### Validation

The November 11 meeting minutes record the demonstration. The commit includes `new_code/test/application-resumes.test.js`, `new_code/test/application-metrics.test.js`, and `new_code/test/sprint3-acceptance.test.js`.

### Related Work

**Repository:** https://github.com/zayum20/Soen-341
**Commit:** `a3551b5`
