## Entry 4 — Sprint 4: AI Job Matching

**Date:** November 23–26, 2026
**Team Member:** Ayza
**AI Tool:** Cursor (Grok)
**Sprint:** 4
**Purpose:** Recommend open jobs from a seeker's skills, experience, education, and preferences.

### Task

I used Cursor to build the second generative-AI feature. It recommends real open postings. It is separate from resume feedback, which reviews one resume against one job the seeker already applied to.

### Prompt / Summary

I asked Cursor to pull the team project, implement job matching, keep the original dashboard, use Gemini to write the reasons, and commit the code without the API key. I later asked why the result showed only the local demo posting.

No public chat link was exported for this Cursor session.

### AI Output Summary

Cursor added the job-matches page, the Job Matches menu link, and the Jobs page link. The server loads at most 12 open jobs, skips archived jobs, expired jobs, and jobs the seeker already applied to, and asks Gemini for job ids, reasons, evidence, and gaps. It drops invented ids, duplicates, and malformed items, then checks that the jobs are still open. Titles and companies come from the database. Tests, `new_code/README-ai-job-matching.md`, and user story US-16 were added.

### Action Taken

**Modified**

I rejected a version that scored jobs locally without Gemini, because the assignment requires the model to write the reasons. I asked to leave the original dashboard unchanged. I asked for the recommendation notes to be shown in boxes. I asked for a partial match to stay on the card, with missing skills listed as gaps. The Gemini model was changed to `gemini-flash-lite-latest` after `gemini-4-hydrogen` returned a temporary unavailable error. The API key stayed in local `.env` and was not committed.

### Validation

I signed in as the local demo seeker and clicked Recommend jobs. Gemini returned the Frontend Intern card with a reason, evidence, and a JavaScript gap, and View job opened that posting. The automated job-matching tests were run, and the notes were checked in the browser. This local database has only that demo posting, so another job appears only after a real posting is added here.

### Related Work

**Repository:** https://github.com/zayum20/Soen-341
**Commit:** `e8eef1e` on `main`
**Related files:** `new_code/server/job-matching.js`, `new_code/server/routes/job-matching.js`, `new_code/public/job-matches.html`, `new_code/README-ai-job-matching.md`
